{"ts": "2026-10-08T02:03:19.651405+00:00", "page_name": "Brazos County TX SO", "portal_status": "active", "portal_last_updated": "2026-10-07T21:46:59.542Z", "overview": "Protecting the people who live, work, and visit Brazos County is at the heart of what we do at the Brazos County Sheriff\u2019s Office. Investigating crime, identifying those responsible, and keeping our community safe are important responsibilities, and we continually look for responsible ways technology can assist us in that mission.\n\nThe Sheriff\u2019s Office uses Flock Safety technology as one of several tools available to our deputies and investigators. The system can assist with criminal investigations by providing objective vehicle information and, in certain circumstances, real-time alerts involving vehicles associated with specific law-enforcement purposes.\n\nThis technology has also assisted our agency in locating missing individuals, helping reunite them with their families and loved ones. These are meaningful outcomes that demonstrate how technology can serve our community beyond traditional criminal investigations.\n\nWe recognize the responsibility that comes with using this technology. Protecting privacy, maintaining strong safeguards, and ensuring Flock is used responsibly are among our highest priorities. These safeguards have been incorporated into our policies and operating procedures to help ensure the technology is used appropriately and for legitimate law-enforcement purposes.", "logo_url": "https://prod-flock-org-files-public.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/transparencyReport/4243f5d9-c261-4d9a-b374-e26c28fdd86f", "hero_image_url": "https://prod-flock-org-files-public.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/transparencyReport/19424f4f-a2a5-45f1-a05f-20b258dd3123", "total_cameras": 10, "searches_30d": 34, "shares_data_with": ["Abilene TX PD", "Amarillo TX PD", "Aubrey TX PD", "Austin County TX SO", "Bay City TX PD", "Bayou Vista TX PD", "Baytown TX PD", "Beaumont TX PD", "Bexar County TX SO",