ock technology utilized by the Brazos County Sheriff\u2019s Office is focused on vehicles and vehicle characteristics. The system captures license plate information and visible characteristics of vehicles, such as make, model, color, and other identifying features that may assist with criminal investigations, locating missing individuals, and other legitimate law-enforcement purposes.", "not_detected": "The Flock technology utilized by the Brazos County Sheriff\u2019s Office is focused on vehicles and vehicle characteristics. It does not collect or identify information about a person\u2019s identity, gender, or race.", "acceptable_use": "Flock data is used by the Brazos County Sheriff\u2019s Office for legitimate law-enforcement purposes, including criminal investigations, locating missing individuals, and other public-safety needs. Access to and use of the system is governed by agency policies and operating procedures designed to ensure the technology is used appropriately and responsibly.", "prohibited_uses": "Flock technology may not be used by the Brazos County Sheriff\u2019s Office for purposes outside of legitimate law-enforcement and public-safety needs. Prohibited uses include:\n\n-Immigration enforcement\n-Issuing traffic citations. The Flock cameras utilized by the Brazos County Sheriff\u2019s Office do not have the capability to issue citations for traffic violations.\n-Harassment, intimidation, or retaliation\n-Targeting or conducting searches based solely on a protected characteristic, including race, sex, religion, or other protected status\n-Personal use or access for reasons unrelated to official law-enforcement duties", "access_policy": "Access to the Flock system is limited to authorized personnel and requires a valid law-enforcement purpose. All searches are logged to support accountability and appropriate use of the system. Search logs are retained indefinitely.", "hotlist_policy": "Flock hotlist alerts are intended to provide an investigative lead and do not, by themselves, provide sufficient grounds for law-enforcement action. Before taking action based on a hotlist alert, deputies must independently verify the alert and confirm that the vehicle and license plate information match the circumstances identified in the alert.\nSOC 2 Type II", "more_info": {"30 Days": "[data-tp-access-viewport=\"true\"]::-webkit-scrollbar {\n                        display: none;\n                    }\n                Abilene TX PD"}}
